*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# A BACKUP OF A CREDENTIALS FILE IS STILL A CREDENTIALS FILE (added 2026-09-02).
# `docs/Credentials.txt` was already ignored above, but a rotation left
# `docs/Credentials.txt.bak-2026-08-30-before-mailbox-pw` sitting untracked in the working tree and
# NOT matched by anything here - one careless `git add .` from being committed. BoatBuddy has no
# user accounts, so the one shared password in that file is the whole door for all three owners.
# Patterned rather than named, so the next rotation's backup is covered without anyone remembering.
docs/Credentials.txt*
**/Credentials.txt*
**/credentials.txt*

# A BACKUP OF ANYTHING IS NEVER SOMETHING `git add .` SHOULD SWEEP UP (added 2026-09-02).
# The fleet's rotation convention is `<name>.bak-YYYY-MM-DD-before-<what>`, so the next
# rotation of ANY file - not only the credentials one - is covered without anyone remembering.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*~

# Playwright OUTPUT. A failing run writes an accessibility snapshot that can contain form
# field VALUES, and CI already uploads playwright-report/ as an artifact; it must never
# ALSO be committable. All four of these are generated, never authored.
playwright-report/
playwright/.gate-a/
test-results/
blob-report/

# The name-based guard that enforces the block above, in CI where nothing can bypass it:
#   node scripts/guard-credential-files.mjs            (audit this repo)
#   node scripts/guard-credential-files.mjs --dir DIR  (audit any directory)
